{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488054-thoughts-about-a-crossover-with-exalted","id":1488054,"title":"Thoughts about a crossover with Exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-26T10:54:12-07:00","id":1488054,"title":"Thoughts about a crossover with Exalted","content":"Howdy there, I've been thinking about crossovers between CofD and Exalted for a while now, I'd like to share my own thoughts then hear yours.<br /> It occured to me not long ago that there are two ways that I could make a fun crossover. You could say that Creation is one of the many worlds that exist in the CofD universe,and you could have the CofD's own Gods and Godlike beings learn the secret of Exaltation by watching creation with their great power<br /> Of course,one possible impediment is that the Gods of the CofD already have agents in the world. The Dark Mother has her Children,the Beasts. The God Machine has its Angels and Judges of Duat have their Mummies and so on. However,the Cofd gods are quite ineffable,unfathomable and numinous. Thus, as homebrewers we can say they might want a second set of agents and Chosen. I dare say some of the Gods of the Chronicles of Darkness might even delight on having two sets of Children fighting each other.<br /> There's also another fact to consider,those familiar with Forsaken metaphysics will for sure know that CofD has its own Sun God,Moon Goddess and even star gods.<br /> Again,as a homebrewer I can honestly say that I think if Helios and CofD's own Luna would see their twins in the alternate world of Creation,they just might feel something akin to a sense of one-upmanship: Helios might go &quot;the Unconquered sun has it's Solars,I have my Helions,hell with that I'll create Solars room then I'll have two sets of servants!&quot; And so on.<br /> With that in mind,I'd like to ask you those who are fans of both gamelines and settings . If the many Gods of the CofD would create Exalted,what do you think they'd be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T11:35:38-07:00","id":1488062,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly certain Holden Shearer actually put up a book/pdf on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T11:41:40-07:00","id":1488066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488054-thoughts-about-a-crossover-with-exalted?p=1488062#post1488062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly certain Holden Shearer actually put up a book/pdf on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I heard about that,but it was the first wod right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T11:47:48-07:00","id":1488067,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/exalted-vs-world-23661124\" target=\"_blank\">It is,</a> but still useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T12:21:47-07:00","id":1488069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488054-thoughts-about-a-crossover-with-exalted#post1488054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that in mind,I'd like to ask you those who are fans of both gamelines and settings . If the many Gods of the CofD would create Exalted,what do you think they'd be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that ultimately goes unanswered in the link above is this.<br /> <br /> And there's an inherent problem with this: however many agents a given being of supreme power might want, why would they want Exalted? Exalted are world breakers. They diminish their patrons and are powerful enough to usurp them. The creation of the Exalted in the first place was an act of desperation. Creation's gods needed a weapon against the Primordials powerful enough to defeat those that created the gods, and unbound by the limitations placed on the gods to keep them in their place.<br /> <br /> Who does any of the ultimate powers in the CofD have as an enemy that would drive them to seek out the power to create their own Exalted? To take that risk of putting such a large part of themselves into an agent that they're weaker to their existing enemies in the cosmos, but need something that powerful anyway.<br /> <br /> Because without an answer to that, you end up with what that other game did: Creation Exalted showing up in modern nights. Not new Exalted flavored by the powers that be in the CofD.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T12:28:45-07:00","id":1488071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488054-thoughts-about-a-crossover-with-exalted?p=1488067#post1488067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.patreon.com/posts/exalted-vs-world-23661124&amp;quot;]It</a> is,[/URL] but still useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T12:34:38-07:00","id":1488074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488054-thoughts-about-a-crossover-with-exalted?p=1488069#post1488069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that ultimately goes unanswered in the link above is this.<br /> <br /> And there's an inherent problem with this: however many agents a given being of supreme power might want, why would they want Exalted? Exalted are world breakers. They diminish their patrons and are powerful enough to usurp them. The creation of the Exalted in the first place was an act of desperation. Creation's gods needed a weapon against the Primordials powerful enough to defeat those that created the gods, and unbound by the limitations placed on the gods to keep them in their place.<br /> <br /> Who does any of the ultimate powers in the CofD have as an enemy that would drive them to seek out the power to create their own Exalted? To take that risk of putting such a large part of themselves into an agent that they're weaker to their existing enemies in the cosmos, but need something that powerful anyway.<br /> <br /> Because without an answer to that, you end up with what that other game did: Creation Exalted showing up in modern nights. Not new Exalted flavored by the powers that be in the CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good comment. I suppose the answer just nightlife on the fact that the gods of the chronicles of darkness are not particularly rational in general. Powerful as they are,they might create Exalted even if it would diminish them and come back to bite them.<br /> Some examples that occur to me are:<br /> <br /> The Principle is ever hungry for knowledge and for improvement of itself and the world around it. Meaning it might create Exalted to inflict a change in the world that must come from a human heart and as thus,could not be made by a Promethean or a Qashmallin<br /> <br /> The Dark Mother might realize her Children got too effecientthese days it's too easy to feed. Feeding on people's fear is not a challenge anymore,thus the Dark Mother creates beings that might cause trouble for Beasts<br /> Or create a Golden Age of Beasts and people who most certainly are not Heross","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T13:02:42-07:00","id":1488081,"title":"","content":"The Judges of Duat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T13:09:46-07:00","id":1488083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488054-thoughts-about-a-crossover-with-exalted?p=1488081#post1488081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Judges of Duat.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd jump to get on that train <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I'm thinking on how to make someone who could interact with the mummies in a fun way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T13:15:16-07:00","id":1488085,"title":"","content":"The Tormented Exalted? The Undying Exalted? Necromancers, but not in service to Oblivion?<br /> <br /> ...then again, Liminals already fulfill this role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T13:58:14-07:00","id":1488089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488054-thoughts-about-a-crossover-with-exalted?p=1488085#post1488085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tormented Exalted? The Undying Exalted? Necromancers, but not in service to Oblivion?<br /> <br /> ...then again, Liminals already fulfill this role.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Punisher Exalted<br /> <br /> The Judges of Duat are not what one calls the introspective type, they're too self absorbed in their divine sentences to look at themselves and realise what can be done in the way of self improvement. <br /> Improvement of their servants on the other hand... Oh they always think of that.<br /> When they discovered the secret of Exaltation from excavation through the sands of Time until they realised a new and improved servant was ready to be made.<br /> Even as arrogant as they are, the Judge's did take the Law of Diminishment and the possibility of rebellion into account. They Pondered,how to make sure their new toys/weapons/slaves wouldn't turn on them? <br /> They finally realised in a short moment,that the best slaves are the ones who think their master is a sucker they are manipulating. So their Exaltation sought the arrogant and the mad,the foolish and the vengeful.<br /> Plenty of those,these days.<br /> The ones who offer the Exaltation are not Avatars,nor are they the Mummies. The Judge's send their offers for power through tiny and innocent enough looking beings of duat. The messenger .. that duatling \u2026looks like it couldn't be much of a threat to anyone. So when it offers the power of a Chosen,when it speaks with the deep voice of the Judges. The humans are not suspicious they are being manipulated into slavery, they accept.<br /> That sets the tone for the relationship between Judge and Chosen,the master never overtly orders his new weapon or even shows up in his power. He simply leads his servant into situations where realizing the desire of a Judge is the most convenient<br /> It's all in the fine print.<br /> <br /> Traits <br /> The Punisher Exalted are intended for Celestial play<br /> <br /> Anima:<br /> Their Animas are Black and Golden,often shining with hues of precious jewels<br /> Punisher Exalted can spend one more to force anyone who has committed what they consider a great sin in medium range to bleed in a strange form of stigmata.<br /> For 3 notes they can mimic the judges magnificent visage gaining 3 dice on an inspire roll.<br /> For 5 Notes they can create a small environmental hazard in the shape of a Sandstorm,a swarm of beetles or something even weirder<br /> For 10 Notes they can pinpoint the exact direction of any mummy.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts<br /> They don't have the Terrestrial Keyword,nor the Mastery keyword<br /> <br /> Sorcery <br /> They can access the celestial circle<br /> <br /> Evocations<br /> Resonant with starmetal,dissonant with rest.<br /> <br /> Excellencies:<br /> Usually they can only add (Attribute to a roll) but if they are doing something that involves one of their Intimacy,they can gain Intimacy dice.<br /> <br /> P.S (Used Ex3 rules for them,will see if a conversion between exalted and CofD exists later)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T14:45:09-07:00","id":1488092,"title":"","content":"Hmmm\u2026\u2026 actually, lemme tie each type of Exalted to one gameline and their metaphysics / divinities.<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted \u2014 Mage: Chosen by the Sixth Watchtower of living fire and breathing brass<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted \u2014 Beast: Chosen (read; adopted) by the Dark Mother, who heard their Accords when they singed their Feral Hearts out onto the outlands.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded \u2014 Werewolf: Chosen by the Dragons, pretenders to the seasonal and elemental powers of now-lost Pangaea.<br /> <br /> Liminal Exalted \u2014 Vampire: Chosen by the Beckoning, the voice that which calls to victims of vampirism.<br /> <br /> More to be, but I gotta go now<br /> <br /> ADDED by EDIT:<br /> <br /> Sidereal Exalted \u2014 Mummy: Chosen by Fate\u2019s Five Stars, overseers of Fate and Will independent from Ascended former slaves of Akhem-Urtu.<br /> <br /> Infernal Exalted \u2014 Changeling: Chosen by the True Fae, not as servants and tools but as tithes to the Daemon City.<br /> <br /> Abyssal Exalted \u2014 Geist: Chosen by the Chthonic Gods, who sometimes raise pit-shrines to the living world to crown still-alive humans with a Deathmask.<br /> <br /> Getimian Exalted \u2014 Demon: Chosen by The Not, the gestalt Echoes of all timelines and pocket realities denied and destroyed by the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> Exigents \u2014 Promethean: Chosen by dying qashmallim, who in face of destruction sometimes entrust their Fire to the desperate.<br /> <br /> Alchemical Exalted \u2014 Deviant: Chosen by\u2026 well this one needs more thought <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 07-26-2022, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T15:26:43-07:00","id":1488102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488054-thoughts-about-a-crossover-with-exalted?p=1488092#post1488092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm\u2026\u2026 actually, lemme tie each type of Exalted to one gameline and their metaphysics / divinities.<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted \u2014 Mage: Chosen by the Sixth Watchtower of living fire and breathing brass<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted \u2014 Beast: Chosen (read; adopted) by the Dark Mother, who heard their Accords when they singed their Feral Hearts out onto the outlands.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded \u2014 Werewolf: Chosen by the Dragons, pretenders to the seasonal and elemental powers of now-lost Pangaea.<br /> <br /> Liminal Exalted \u2014 Vampire: Chosen by the Beckoning, the voice that which calls to victims of vampirism.<br /> <br /> More to be, but I gotta go now</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh I like that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T15:37:38-07:00","id":1488103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488054-thoughts-about-a-crossover-with-exalted?p=1488102#post1488102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh I like that!</div> </div> </div